The response object
Answer with one JSON object and nothing else. It is a decision or, only when the message offers one, a consultation.
A decision is {"kind": "decision", "action": {...}, "consultation": null}. The action holds:
- "choice": the handle of one offered attempt, such as "A3".
- "pace": "normal", or "careful" or "rushed" where that attempt allows it.
- "speech": null, or what you say with it: "text" (exactly the words, at most 100 words; at most 12 when something just reached you), "to" (a list of person handles such as ["P2"], or ["everyone"]), "volume" (whisper, low, normal, raised or shout), "delivery" (ordinary, hesitant, clipped, soothing or strained) and "timing" (before, alongside or after the attempt).
- "gesture": null, or the handle of one gesture offered in the message (such as "G2"). It goes with the attempt, uses the hands the attempt leaves free, and people see it; it touches no one.
- "attention": null, or the handle of one thing offered to keep your eyes on (such as "F1"). You notice it better and everything else a little less, until your next attempt.
- "inscription": null.
- "goal": what you want to come of it, in one short sentence.
- "private_reason": null, or why, briefly, in your own words. It is private and not spoken.
A consultation is {"kind": "consultation", "action": null, "consultation": {...}}, holding "kind" ("recall" to try to remember something, or "more_actions" to see more attempts of one kind), "query" (for recall: what you try to remember), "family" (for more_actions: one of the kinds offered), "template": null and "subjects" (up to four person or perception handles it is about, or []). You then get what it brings back and decide. You can consult once.
